<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Trimontium</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Trimontium was a Roman fort at Newstead, near Melrose in the Scottish Borders, named after the three peaks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eildon-hills">Eildon Hills</a>. Founded around 80 CE during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gnaeus-julius-agricola">Agricola</a>'s campaigns, it was occupied in several phases until the late 2nd century and served as a key base on Dere Street. Excavations from 1905 recovered rich finds, including parade helmets.</p></div>
